# build/ holds BOTH the scripts that drive the build and everything those scripts produce. Ignoring the whole directory
# meant tinycc, cc-one.sh, build-ggml-cuda.sh, link-null.sh, link-llama-bench.sh, sdk.sh and fetch-cuda-headers.sh -
# every one of them named in the README's Layout section - were never committed. A fresh clone of this repository could
# not build, and the move to a new machine on 2026-09-17 carried them only because it was a file copy and not a clone.
# So: the outputs stay ignored, the scripts do not. Note this must be `build/*` and not `build/`, because a negation
# cannot reach inside a directory git has been told to ignore entirely.
build/*
!build/*.sh
!build/tinycc
*.o
*.a
*.dSYM/
cuda-13
*.fatbin
*.cu.cpp
spike/spike
spike/spike_real
libtinynv/third_party
spike/*.cubin
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# NOTE: the two rules above deliberately have no trailing slash. A worktree needs these paths symlinked in
# (they are large, fetched, and shared), and a `dir/` rule matches a directory but NOT a symlink standing
# where that directory would be - so the symlink is committable, and one nearly was, carrying an absolute
# path to one machine's checkout. Without the slash both the real directory and a symlink are ignored.
.DS_Store
